  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Asiane</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Karia was a geographic region of the Roman Empire whose territory belonged to the province of Asia. As a part of the Diocletianic reforms, Karia was subdivided into smaller units. It again became a separate province as part of the Diocese of Asia.",
